<template>
    <children>
        <li id="34.lp5"/>
        <li id="33.lp5"/>
        <li id="32.lp5"/>
    </children>
    <heading>Model</heading>
    <keywords>
        <li>model</li>
        <li>project</li>
        <li>directory handle</li>
        <li>IndexedDB</li>
    </keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p><code>window.LP5.model</code> owns the current directory handle privately; it exposes no getter for that handle. Its interface is <code>await model.selectProject(handle)</code>, which stores the supplied handle in IndexedDB and then installs it as the current selection. It returns no handle.</p>
        <p>Selection delegates persistence to <code>util.indexedDB.storeDirectoryHandle(handle)</code>. Previously selected directories remain available in the persistent set. If storage fails, the Promise rejects and the current in-memory selection is preserved.</p>
        <p>The selected handle is used by <code>loadProject()</code>, described in the child articles. Restoring saved selections and checking permissions remain later work. The model does not open the picker or perform UI work.</p>
